1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,696
You find a flight for 170 euros.

2
00:00:02,696 --> 00:00:05,263
A day later, the same seat costs 260.

3
00:00:05,263 --> 00:00:08,150
Or you book, and the next morning it's cheaper.

4
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:11,950
CapFare locks the price of your flight, wherever you book.

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:13,150
It runs on NEAR.

6
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:16,275
The extension recognises the flight on

7
00:00:16,275 --> 00:00:20,150
any booking site and offers to lock a maximum price.

8
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:24,050
A passkey creates a readable NEAR account.

9
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,150
No seed phrase, no gas, prepaid credit.

10
00:00:27,950 --> 00:00:31,574
The premium comes from a public formula on-chain.

11
00:00:31,574 --> 00:00:35,650
The maximum payout is locked in the vault first.

12
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:42,150
Choose the deductible and a lock of three to thirty days.

13
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,603
When the demo price passes your cap,

14
00:00:45,603 --> 00:00:48,255
you get an alert in the app,

15
00:00:48,255 --> 00:00:50,150
by push or by email.

16
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:53,283
Claim with the original email.

17
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:56,083
The payout waits for a live

18
00:00:56,083 --> 00:00:59,350
check of the booking after a day,

19
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:02,150
then it's paid from the vault.

20
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:06,834
Only the flight, fare and price reach the chain.

21
00:01:06,834 --> 00:01:11,150
Edited emails, reused bookings and other people's bookings are refused.

22
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:15,050
Just booked? The Drop Guarantee pays

23
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:18,150
if the same flight gets cheaper.

24
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:21,915
Route cover pays against the cheapest fare,

25
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:26,150
up to three days either side and from nearby airports.

26
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:30,050
Up to nine travellers on one policy,

27
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:33,150
and a return trip bought as one.

28
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:37,550
Liquidity providers fund two vaults.

29
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:41,150
Every policy is fully collateralised.

30
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:46,897
Why NEAR? Gasless meta-transactions through our relayer,

31
00:01:46,897 --> 00:01:49,723
and readable named accounts.

32
00:01:49,723 --> 00:01:56,790
NEP-141 tokens, async cross-contract calls that roll back on failure,

33
00:01:56,790 --> 00:01:59,617
and ed25519 checks on-chain.

34
00:01:59,617 --> 00:02:03,150
All on the public explorer.

35
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:08,064
It's a testnet prototype: live contracts, demo prices,

36
00:02:08,064 --> 00:02:11,150
services not in an enclave yet.

37
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:16,150
CapFare. Built at the NEAR Hackathon.
